-- Who performs an action is read from its record in the order the record
-- DECLARES its fields: the subject-first canon (see regulative-actor-duplex.l4).
-- A named construction does not have to write its fields in that order, so the
-- performer is the party in the FIRST DECLARED party field, whatever was written
-- first.
--
-- Here `sender` is declared first, so Bob performs `reordered` although
-- `recipient IS Alice` is written before `sender IS Bob`. The same record given
-- by position, `Msg OF Bob, Alice, "yo"`, has always been performed by Bob.
-- The mirror image, each action under the other party, is in
-- not-ok/tc/regulative-performer-declared-order.l4.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob

DECLARE Msg HAS
    sender    IS A Person
    recipient IS A Person
    body      IS A STRING

GIVETH A Msg
reordered MEANS Msg WITH recipient IS Alice, sender IS Bob, body IS "yo"

GIVETH A Msg
positional MEANS Msg OF Bob, Alice, "yo"

GIVETH A PROVISION OF Person, Msg
fromReordered MEANS PARTY Bob MUST reordered WITHIN 1

GIVETH A PROVISION OF Person, Msg
fromPositional MEANS PARTY Bob MUST positional WITHIN 1
